# Build context exclusions for the backend image.
#
# The backend builds with `context: ./backend` (see docker-compose.yml),
# so the repo-root .dockerignore does NOT apply here — that one only
# covers the frontend and multiplayer images, which build from `.`.
# Without this file every path below lands in the image via `COPY . .`.

# Secrets. A developer's real .env — database URL, SECRET_KEY,
# ENCRYPTION_KEY, cloud credentials — otherwise ships inside any image
# built from a configured checkout, readable by anyone who can pull it.
# The container gets its configuration from the environment at runtime.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime-written user uploads (QA evidence, bug attachments) under the
# local-disk storage backend. Shipping one developer's uploads to every
# deployment is wrong on its own, and their presence in the context
# also masks a real bug: it makes /app/data/uploads exist at build time
# by accident, so the missing-mountpoint permission failure reproduces
# on a clean build but not on the machine that last ran the app.
data/

# Local virtualenv and tooling caches — rebuilt in the image, and on a
# host with a different platform the venv's binaries are unusable.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.log
